// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (R-VSTORE, review round 4, B7; the bad twin): the
// closure stores a reference into a capture before its task starts, so the
// call keeps the rule of main (root: issue #104). The probe of the review:
// Review probe Z9c-B r4: a function makes r point into its vector by a closure that it calls; the task of the closure pushes the vector.
fn work(w: Vec<u64>) / async {
    let u = Vec.new()
    u.push(5)
    let r = &u[0]
    let g = || w.push(2)
    let f = || { r = &w[0]; scope { s => s.spawn(g); () } }
    f()
    print(r)
}
fn main() / async {
    let w = Vec.new()
    w.push(1)
    work(w)
}
